<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see snow, cold temperatures.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see snow, cold temperatures.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Wednesday were forecast to see cold temperatures and snow in the east, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see a mix of sun and cloud with highs of 0 to -4.0 Celsius. More than 85 percent of Alberta's harvest was completed by Monday, Alberta Agriculture said.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see sunny skies and highs of -14 to -8.0 Celsius. Harvest was 94 percent completed by Monday, Saskatchewan Agriculture said.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see snow and highs of -10 to -5.0 Celsius. Harvest was almost completed, Manitoba Agriculture said.</p>
<p>--Gilbert Le Gras 204-947-3548</p>
</text>
